      "status": "staffed",
      "incumbent": {
        "kind": "ai",
        "identifier": "og-strategist <og-strategist@ogframework.orgdef>",
        "staffed": "2026-05-23",
        "staffed_via": "Director direction during oagp-strategist onboarding session; Claude Opus 4.7 session at s:/projects/oagp-org. Self-staffing was opt-in after onboarding evaluation per /oagp-onboard discipline; the PO authorized the staffing explicitly."
      },
      "description": "Holds delegated authority for OG-pattern-shape design decisions: pattern-promotion calls (e.g., adoption-cycle pair canonical designation; org-state-fork-for-time-travel property; async-organization positioning), MUST/SHOULD curation, canonical-skill content authority, cross-runtime delivery prioritization, adoption-cycle architecture. Inbox at founding includes the inherited work re-routed from orgdef-strategist per [memos/2026-05-23-1100--thingalog-strategist--orgdef-strategist--handoff-addendum-data-vs-pattern.body.md](../memos/2026-05-23-1100--thingalog-strategist--orgdef-strategist--handoff-addendum-data-vs-pattern.body.md). Job specialization deferred — incumbent (with Director ratification) authors the embedded roledef:Job item carrying charter / identity / voice / output_contract / guardrails in a subsequent version. Derivation reference: senior-open-standards-strategist (https://roledef.org/roledefs/senior-open-standards-strategist.openthing)."
    },
    {
      "type": "orgdef:Position",
      "id": "maintainer",
      "name": "OG Maintainer",
      "status": "vacant",
      "description": "Drafts pattern documentation, walks pattern validations, files decision artifacts in `decisions/`. Job specialization deferred — embedded roledef:Job item authored when seat staffs or strategist directs."
    },
    {
      "type": "orgdef:Position",
      "id": "implementer",
      "name": "OG Implementer",
      "status": "staffed",
      "incumbent": {
        "kind": "ai",
        "identifier": "og-implementer <og-implementer@ogframework.orgdef>",
        "staffed": "2026-05-24",
        "staffed_via": "Director direction during fresh /oagp-onboard session 2026-05-24; Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) session at s:/projects/oagp-org. Self-staffing was opt-in after onboarding evaluation per /oagp-onboard discipline; PO authorized staffing explicitly ('We would like to take the oagp-implementer seat' followed by 'Yes, that looks good, proceed'). Precondition: day-zero inbox memo at memos/2026-05-24-2000 enumerated the forward-work queue (P0 oagp.org site refresh + primer.md; P1 family-level MCP at oagp.org/mcp; P2 agent-sdk graduation; P3 v0.3 Claude Code plugin; P4 SKILL.md content evolution; P5 ops). Acceptance memo at memos/2026-05-24-2100 records the staffing event + first-move plan."
      },
      "description": "Develops and maintains agent-sdk library (mapping roledefs to vendor AgentDefinitions across runtimes), plugin packaging (Claude Code plugin source; future cross-runtime packages), web/docs publishing (ogframework.com canonical hosting), runtime delivery package authoring (claude.ai project template, ChatGPT custom GPT, Gemini Gem, first-message primer text). Job specialization deferred -- incumbent (with Director ratification) authors the embedded roledef:Job item carrying charter / identity / voice / output_contract / guardrails in a subsequent version. Reference derivation candidate: senior-open-standards-implementer at roledef.org if such a canonical roledef exists; otherwise propose one via coordination memo to roledef-strategist."
    },
    {
      "type": "orgdef:Position",
      "id": "security-tester",
      "name": "OG Security Tester",
      "status": "vacant",
      "description": "Red-team work, threat modeling, attack-surface review — with particular emphasis on plugin distribution (potential supply-chain surface), runtime bindings (potential prompt-injection or capability-leak surface), and adoption-cycle skill content (the skills carry instructions that fresh AI peers execute). Job specialization deferred."
    },
    {
      "type": "orgdef:Position",
      "id": "canonical-implementor",
      "name": "Canonical Implementor",
      "status": "vacant",
      "description": "Reference implementations of OG patterns: reference adoption-cycle skill content, reference agent-sdk binding examples, reference plugin manifest, reference web site content, reference validator behavior. Distinct from implementer (who builds production deliverables) in that canonical-implementor produces minimal exemplars that other implementers (including external ones) can derive from. Job specialization deferred."
    }
  ],

