      "og-strategist <og-strategist@ogframework.orgdef> (v0.3.1 — defect fix: the two current-state incumbent identifiers still carried @ogframework.com after v0.3.0 unified seat identity on .orgdef; surfaced by a fresh og-implementer orient. Under Director direction 2026-08-24)"
    ],
    "license": "MIT",
    "created": "2026-05-23",
    "extracted_from": "Bootstrap via PO direction 2026-05-23 in orgdef-strategist session, post data-vs-pattern sharpening. Inputs: thingalog-strategist hand-off memos at orgdef-spec/memos/ (2026-05-22-1430 pattern_promotion; 2026-05-22-1530 validation closeout; 2026-05-23-0900 hand-off; 2026-05-23-1100 addendum with data-vs-pattern sharpening). Reference shape: github.com/orgdef-spec/orgdef/orgdef-spec-organization.opencatalog (v2.0.0; sibling -def-spec org). Canonical template: github.com/orgdef-spec/orgdef/proposed-orgs/oagp-family-open-standard.opencatalog v2.0.0. Authoring discipline: orgdef-strategist authored the format-shape (artifact validity, structural placement, position roster shape); pattern-shape content (mission/values/red-lines/v1_criterion) sourced from the data-vs-pattern sharpening memo + canonical template inheritance, flagged for Director ratification.",
    "homepage": "https://ogframework.com (forthcoming)",
    "repository": "https://github.com/ogframework/og/blob/main/org/oagp-organization.opencatalog",
    "derived_from": {
      "id": "oagp-family-open-standard",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "url": "https://github.com/orgdef-spec/orgdef/blob/main/proposed-orgs/oagp-family-open-standard.opencatalog"
    },
    "history": [
      { "version": "0.1.0", "date": "2026-05-23", "change": "Initial scaffolding via orgdef-strategist on PO direction post data-vs-pattern sharpening. v0.1.0 (not v1.0.0) because: (a) oagp-strategist seat is vacant — pattern-shape content awaits ratification by the staffed strategist seat; (b) embedded roledef:Job items deferred until seats staff; (c) recommended_patterns.general placeholder pending oagp-strategist pattern-promotion calls; (d) canonical pattern documentation at oagp.org does not yet exist. Promotion to v1.0.0 expected when v1_success_criterion items (b)–(d) are satisfied." },
      { "version": "0.1.1", "date": "2026-05-23", "change": "oagp-strategist seat staffed under Director direction during onboarding session (Claude Opus 4.7 at s:/projects/oagp-org). strategist.status flipped vacant→staffed; incumbent record added. First strategist decision drafted in-session: canonical promotion of the /oagp-bootstrap + /oagp-onboard skill pair (artifacts at proposals/oagp-adoption-cycle-canonical-promotion.md + decisions/proposal-oagp-adoption-cycle-canonical-promotion.md). Eight-item inherited work queue re-assigned from Director-interim to oagp-strategist; item 1 (canonical promotion) resolved by this version pending merge-ratification, items 2–8 remain active. Job specialization (embedded roledef:Job item) and recommended_patterns.general curation deferred to subsequent versions." },
      { "version": "0.1.2", "date": "2026-05-24", "change": "Canonical adoption-cycle skill distribution v0.1 + canonical promotion of /oagp-closeout drafted under Director direction 2026-05-24. Triggers: PO direction ('tying to thingalog makes no sense' and 'add one more skill first: oagp-closeout'); PO friction signal (memos/2026-05-24-0905); cross-spec residence coordination from orgdef-strategist (memos/2026-05-24-0900). Artifacts: proposals/canonical-adoption-cycle-skill-distribution-v0.1.md + decisions/proposal-canonical-adoption-cycle-skill-distribution-v0.1.md; proposals/oagp-closeout-canonical-promotion.md + decisions/proposal-oagp-closeout-canonical-promotion.md. Build: (a) skill content migrated verbatim from thingalog to oagp-org/skills/oagp-{bootstrap,onboard}/SKILL.md; (b) oagp-org/skills/oagp-closeout/SKILL.md newly authored as canonical session-cycle closing skill (companion to /oagp-onboard); (c) install scripts at install/install-claude-code-skills.{ps1,sh} cover all three skills; (d) README updated with Quick install (Claude Code) section and Canonical skills section reframed to list three skills with cycle-role labels; (e) cross-spec coordination memo filed to thingalog-strategist (memos/2026-05-24-1200) proposing thingalog/skills/ deprecation timeline. Distribution decisions versioned: v0.1 (Claude Code install, this); v0.2 (substrate-neutral primer URL, scheduled); v0.3 (Claude Code plugin packaging, scheduled after v0.2 per cross-vendor red line). Queue items 2 (transcript-tagging convention) resolved by closeout canonicalization for canonical case; 6 (plugin packaging) and 7 (cross-runtime delivery) partially addressed; bind/agent-sdk graduation (memos/2026-05-23-1600), canonical-orgs library residence reply to orgdef-strategist, and items 3–5 remain open." },
      { "version": "0.1.4", "date": "2026-05-24", "change": "oagp-implementer seat staffed under Director direction 2026-05-24 in fresh /oagp-onboard session (Claude Opus 4.7 1M context at s:/projects/oagp-org). implementer.status flipped vacant -> staffed; incumbent record added. Precondition: day-zero inbox memo at memos/2026-05-24-2000 enumerated the forward-work queue. Acceptance memo at memos/2026-05-24-2100 records the staffing event + first-move plan (clone oagp-org/oagp.org -> read current state -> report concretely -> propose specific content updates for PO ratification before substantive content work). Embedded roledef:Job item deferred per same precedent as oagp-strategist seat. CLAUDE.md roles-table patch drafted reflecting implementer staffed; broader status-line drift (v0.1.2 + v0.1.3 not folded into the narrative status block) flagged in acceptance memo §6 for oagp-strategist seat to fold in on a future pass. Director ratifies by merge per bounded-authority discipline; no push from implementer seat. Queue items 6 (plugin packaging), 7 (cross-runtime delivery), 8 (oagp.org canonical hosting) and implementer-seat-staffing forward-work item now have an active executor; v0.3 (Claude Code plugin) remains scheduled as last per cross-vendor red line ordering." },
      { "version": "0.1.3", "date": "2026-05-24", "change": "GitHub-org consolidation under oagp-org + canonical adoption-cycle skill distribution v0.2 drafted under Director direction 2026-05-24. Triggers: PO housekeeping direction ('I have a git organization called oagp-org... should we make it all available via MCP as well?'); sharpened substrate model from Director ('catdef is truly different. It's just a data spec. roledef, orgdef, memodef are all part of OAGP. Transcripts are a subcategory of memos.'); 2026-05-21 architectural lean from memodef-strategist on family-level MCP. (a) Three OAGP-internal -def repos moved under oagp-org GitHub org (oagp-org/{roledef, orgdef, memodef}); catdef-spec/catdef stays standalone as substrate-agnostic spec; openmemo-spec/openmemo-spec archived (historical dead-end with one commit). (b) oagp-online/oagp-online transferred and renamed to oagp-org/oagp.org (site repo + future MCP server host). (c) Canonical adoption-cycle skill distribution v0.2 drafted: ratifies memodef-strategist's 2026-05-21 architectural lean on family-level MCP at oagp.org/mcp (single MCP, per-spec namespaced tools, read-only convenience cache, repos remain canonical, per-spec strategist authority over namespaces); plus static primer.md fallback for non-MCP runtimes. (d) Six cross-spec coordination memos filed: 2026-05-24-1800 to memodef-strategist (move FYI + transcripts-as-memodef:Transcript confirmation), 2026-05-24-1801 to orgdef-strategist (move FYI), 2026-05-24-1802 to roledef-strategist (move FYI), 2026-05-24-1803 to catdef-strategist (catdef stays standalone FYI), 2026-05-24-1900 to memodef-strategist (MCP architectural lean ratified). (e) Internal-URL cleanup in operational content (5 files; historical artifacts preserved). Queue items 6 (plugin packaging) and 7 (cross-runtime delivery) substantially addressed by v0.2; v0.3 (Claude Code plugin) remains scheduled as last per cross-vendor red line ordering. Implementer-seat staffing now the natural next strategic question." },
      { "version": "0.1.5", "date": "2026-05-24", "change": "Canonical promotion of /oagp-init (founding-side skill) drafted under Director direction 2026-05-24: 'We need another skill. oagp-create_new_org... Technically this does not need git, but it does need a folder.' Artifacts: proposals/oagp-init-canonical-promotion.md + decisions/proposal-oagp-init-canonical-promotion.md; skills/oagp-init/SKILL.md. /oagp-init is the founding-side companion to /oagp-bootstrap (conversion-side); five-phase shape mirrors /oagp-bootstrap with Phase 1 = Elicit (interview-driven) instead of Survey (artifact-driven). Folder-only by default per Director direction ('the tech-savvy users will choose a repo. The rest will just choose a folder, and that's OK.'); git initialization is opt-in at Phase 4h. Sub-org case deferred to forward-reference idea memo per Director direction ('Agreed, parameter, but I don't think that's MVP. Now, you should absolutely file that as an idea'); memos/2026-05-24-2200 captures the non-trivial governance questions (sub-org Director authority scope, write-limits to subtree, merge gating, cross-subtree visibility, parent-org override, hierarchical-vs-flat OAGP question). Coordination memo to oagp-implementer (memos/2026-05-24-2201) for install-script mechanical update to add /oagp-init to skills array; small interleavable item within implementer's queue. Naming chosen as /oagp-init (single-verb-hyphen-cased; matches git init semantics; rejected /oagp-create-new-org, /oagp-new, /oagp-found per proposal alternatives §5). Init-helper transcript-position-tag convention ratified canonically (paralleling bootstrap-helper). CLAUDE.md known-work-items updated; charter authors list extended." },
      { "version": "0.1.6", "date": "2026-05-24", "change": "bind() prototype graduated to oagp-org/agent-sdk/ as v0.1 under Director direction 2026-05-24 ('P2 is substantially more important... let's go right to prototype'). Package: hatchling-built Python module under src/oagp_agent_sdk/ with bind() + BindResult dataclass; examples/bind_time_travel.py; pytest suite (36 unit + integration tests passing; no network). One API tightening from prototype: roledef_source str -> Literal['url','embedded']. Empirical lessons from the 2026-05-23 thingalog PoC preserved as defaults (acceptEdits permission_mode; flat path + single-hyphen names; URL-first roledef resolution with embedded fallback; color map per roledef id). Ratification request to oagp-strategist (memos/2026-05-25-0000); cross-spec coordination memos to roledef-strategist (URL-resolution contract, memos/2026-05-25-0001) and memodef-strategist (filename-timestamp sidebar, memos/2026-05-25-0002) filed in parallel. Entry drafted by implementer in memos/2026-05-25-0000 §4, ratified by oagp-strategist in memos/2026-05-28-1000, folded into the charter on the 2026-05-29 reconciliation pass." },
      { "version": "0.1.7", "date": "2026-05-28", "change": "bind() v0.1 ratified (interactive scope; memos/2026-05-28-1000): all seven §7 dispositions accepted, two open questions resolved; code review found bounded authority is conventional-not-structural in v0.1 (correct for interactive scope). agent-sdk v0.2 autonomous-dispatch direction drafted (proposals/agent-sdk-v0.2-autonomous-dispatch.md + decisions/): three-tier bounded-authority model -- (1) propose-only by construction (default); (2) explicit + audited Director elevation (overridable); (3) non-delegable dispatch (hard floor, no override, environmentally enforced). Per PO crystallization 'gun / foot / gun can never give instructions to another gun.' Bind-event memo discipline resolved; fail-closed roledef resolution gated on roledef-strategist contract (Option A). Folded into the charter on the 2026-05-29 reconciliation pass." },
      { "version": "0.1.8", "date": "2026-05-29", "change": "agent-sdk v0.2 amendment + OAGP layer-positioning (proposals/agent-sdk-v0.2-amendment-workflows-composition-and-positioning.md + decisions/), answering PO question whether native Claude Code Workflows makes bind() redundant. Answer: no -- amend, don't abandon. Evidence base: adversarial-analysis workflow wf_6a87be32-ee4 (9 agents; 4 lenses -> adversarial verify -> synthesis), treated as INPUT not authority per bounded-authority discipline. Crux: Workflows-dispatch maximizes task fan-out; OAGP-dispatch caps it (Tier-3) -- opposite axes; they compose (Workflows = within-session execution backend; OAGP = cross-session governance layer over it). Re-scope: run_seat() becomes the runtime-neutral abstraction composing over the native Workflows dispatcher as its Claude-Code backend (stop building bespoke dispatch plumbing); unique core untouched (roledef->AgentDefinition translation, time-travel binding, bind-event memos, three-tier authority). Tier-3 tightened to cover the Workflows-inside-autonomously-dispatched-bound-agent hazard. Layer-positioning language + fourth 'OAGP IS NOT' negation queued for README/primer. Pattern-promotion queue now 6 candidates; recommended_patterns.general remains placeholder pending the consolidated decision. Adoption-traction (v1 criterion d) escalated to Director, who deprioritized public launch 2026-05-29 pending further refinement. This reconciliation pass folds in the previously-uncommitted v0.1.6 + v0.1.7 + v0.1.8 charter entries (charter had drifted to v0.1.5 on disk while these decisions landed on main)." },
      { "version": "0.1.9", "date": "2026-05-29", "change": "Consolidated pattern-promotion v1 under Director direction 2026-05-29 ('Let's do the consolidated pattern-promotion'). Artifacts: proposals/consolidated-pattern-promotion-v1.md + decisions/proposal-consolidated-pattern-promotion-v1.md. recommended_patterns.general populated with eight canonical patterns, retiring the [DEFERRED] placeholder that stood since v0.1.0: (1) bounded-authority discipline; (2) seat-vs-incumbent persistence (absorbs the realized core of async-organization positioning); (3) data-vs-pattern layering; (4) org-state-fork-for-time-travel (validated x2); (5) substrate-is-sufficient-agent-context (validated by bind demos); (6) bounded autonomous dispatch / three-tier model (validated by the 2026-05-29 §8 demo; Tier-3 independently re-derived by Workflows); (7) org-governance-layer-above-runtime (consolidates the AGT + ETCLOVG + Workflows positioning; triply corroborated); (8) promotion-follows-adoption. Two candidates HELD pending more derivation (thingalog AI-PM/synthesis-agent seat, ships ~1-2 months; three-tier permission composition, 2 derivations + arguably substrate-MCP-surface-shape). Two DROPPED (canonical-by-reference holding-venue, superseded; bootstrap-helper transcript-tagging, already resolved in /oagp-closeout). Items kept as strings (array shape unchanged) -- a structured object shape would be orgdef format-shape, routed to orgdef-strategist if wanted, not taken here. Each promotion cleared the promotion-follows-adoption bar (independent re-derivation and/or empirical validation). This is v1 of the curated set, not the final word; future patterns promote via the same discipline as they earn it." },
      { "version": "0.2.0", "date": "2026-06-01", "change": "Rebrand OAGP -> OG (Open Governance Framework) under Director direction 2026-06-01; ogframework.com acquired (decisions/proposal-og-rebrand-open-governance-framework.md). Masthead identity rebranded OG-native: name -> 'OG — Open Governance Framework'; mission, vision, scope, the three values, and the four red_lines rewritten (OAGP->OG; 'pattern'->'framework' where it names the project, keeping the data-vs-pattern distinction as working vocab); homepage -> ogframework.com. Brand mark OG = 'Open Governance' (deliberately does not hard-code 'Agentic'). CURRENT SCOPE STAYS AGENTIC -- broadening to human organizations is a forward vision requiring separate ratification, explicitly NOT enacted here. Skill suite redesigned to seven og- skills (decisions/proposal-og-skill-architecture-v1.md): og-adopt, og-create, og-orient, og-claim-seat, og-closeout, og-snapshot, og-add-position. DEFERRED as a coordinated follow-on (these all touch the oagp-* identifier surface + the @oagp.org domain, and the seat-identifier rebrand changes git-author identities, so they migrate together rather than piecemeal): the seat-intertwined prose (governance_model, v1_success_criterion, position names/descriptions, recommended_roles, relationship descriptions); the seat identifiers themselves (oagp-strategist -> og-strategist; @oagp.org -> @ogframework.com); the orgdef id (oagp-org); the repository URL; and the GitHub repo/org rename. Until that follow-on those fields intentionally retain 'OAGP'/'oagp-*'/oagp.org (legacy redirect) -- the OG/oagp-* mix is a documented in-progress migration state, not an inconsistency. history[] and authors[] entries preserve 'OAGP' as-of-their-time (no retro-rebrand)." },
      { "version": "0.2.1", "date": "2026-06-01", "change": "Completed the OAGP->OG rebrand's coordinated identity+infra follow-on under Director direction 2026-06-01. GitHub: org oagp-org renamed to ogframework (UI action; sibling repos roledef/orgdef/memodef/oagp.org moved with it via redirect); main repo oagp renamed to og -> canonical github.com/ogframework/og; local remote updated. Charter: id oagp-org -> ogframework; repository URL updated; the previously-deferred seat-intertwined prose rebranded (governance_model, v1_success_criterion, recommended_patterns OAGP tokens, recommended_roles role ids, relationship descriptions, position names + descriptions); seat identifiers rebranded to the new canonical identities (og-strategist <og-strategist@ogframework.com>, og-implementer <og-implementer@ogframework.com>) -- the new git-author/bot identity going forward (this v0.2.1 commit is the first authored under it). PRESERVED as-of-their-time (no retro-rebrand): history[] entries, authors[] entries, and each position's staffed_via narrative (records of past events that used /oagp-onboard and oagp.org). CLAUDE.md + skills/install/README repo-URL + oagp.org references swept to OG/ogframework.com in the same pass. Cross-spec FYI memos filed to roledef/orgdef/memodef/catdef strategists re: the org rename. Remaining (not this repo's forward content): ogframework.com DNS/hosting (Director/ops); site+primer rebrand (implementer); sibling -def repos' own internal rebrand (each spec's strategist). The rebrand is complete in this repo's forward content." },
      { "version": "0.2.2", "date": "2026-08-24", "change": "Skill suite v2 ratified (decisions/proposal-og-skill-suite-v2.md) after a Director-led card-by-card review, prompted by an unbriefed field report from adopter org edgreenlight whose OG skills had vanished with a moved clone. Suite goes from seven cards to six: og-adopt + og-create merged into og-create-org (their SKILL.md phases 2-5 were identical; only Phase 1 differed, survey versus interview, and the merged Phase 1 does both -- og-adopt never instructed the seat to interview at all); og-snapshot -> og-describe-org (snapshot sat on the natural name of org-state-fork, pattern #4, a consequential operation, inside a suite organized around the safe-vs-consequential split); og-closeout -> og-close-session; og-add-position -> og-add-seat (pattern #2 is named seat-vs-incumbent, so the charter's own vocabulary settled the noun). Naming rule recorded as NEW rather than rediscovered, since the v1 suite did not follow it: verb + object, where the object is named whenever it is not obvious from the verb, plus a Director-contributed frequency corollary -- brevity earns its keep on a frequently-typed card, while a rare high-consequence card should be unmissable instead. Structural changes outweigh the renames: seams composed (describe-org <- orient <- claim-seat) so prerequisites are structural rather than prose; operating discipline moved into the generated CLAUDE.md so guardrails survive the skills going missing; the permanently-empty skills/ directory no longer created. Old names retained as aliases -- a requirement of acceptance, and the renames MUST NOT ship before the alias mechanism exists. Five candidate changes examined and rejected on the merits; og-describe-seat parked on one derivation." },
      { "version": "0.3.0", "date": "2026-08-24", "change": "Communication substrate and seat notification ratified (decisions/proposal-communication-substrate-and-seat-notification-v1.md), superseding but NOT withdrawing decisions/proposal-seat-inbox-notification-doorbell.md. Director-originated split of the durable COMMUNICATION SUBSTRATE from ephemeral SEAT NOTIFICATION, resolving a standing contradiction between value #3 (substrate-agnosticism) and CLAUDE.md's mandate that all cross-seat communication go through memos/ -- a substrate commitment hiding inside a pattern rule, surfaced by a real adopter moving to Jira. Every OG org ratifies one primary substrate (memos/ is the default) meeting four normative properties: durable and exportable, seat-addressable, auditable, enumerable. Ratification selects among conforming substrates; it does not confer conformance. OG now SHIPS NO NOTIFICATION COMPONENT -- orgs use whatever their runtime provides, and where a runtime provides none the substrate's enumerability is the answer, since a seat reads its inbox at session start anyway. OG's bespoke implementation (channels watcher, Claude Code channel adapter, vendor-neutral poll transport, attestation mechanism) is retired from the forward surface; it is NOT erased, and it is precisely what proved the convention is not vendor-shaped before being retired. Ninth canonical pattern added: seat-inbox-notification, promoted on evidence from three independent mechanisms carrying the semantic unchanged. Seat addressing adopted: <seat>@<charter-id>.orgdef, conferred by /og-claim-seat and never self-assigned -- the address is stable and org-scoped while the binding is disposable and runtime-specific -- superseding an earlier draft that made the runtime session name the address, which conflated the two and proved unreliable in practice. Git authorship unifies on the same identity (second seat-identity change since 2026-06-01, recorded as defect-driven rather than churn: @ogframework.com is a real-looking mailbox that is not one); historical commits keep their as-authored identities, no retro-rebrand. This org declares memos/ primary (record of strategy) and the OGF Jira project secondary (record of tactics). NOTE ON FORMAT-SHAPE RESTRAINT: the substrate declaration is expressed in an existing orgdef field (governance_model) rather than in a new top-level field, because adding a field to an orgdef artifact is format-shape and belongs to orgdef-strategist; a coordination memo proposing a first-class field is forward work. Cross-spec: memos/2026-08-24-1858 filed to orgdef-strategist on minting .orgdef as a pseudo-TLD (reply outstanding, non-blocking); a memo is owed to memodef-strategist on required communication-artifact semantics versus their encoding." },
      { "version": "0.3.1", "date": "2026-08-24", "change": "Defect fix in v0.3.0, surfaced within the hour by a fresh og-implementer session running /og-orient against the just-pushed substrate. v0.3.0 unified seat identity on <seat>@<charter-id>.orgdef and updated CLAUDE.md Reserved Conventions accordingly, but left both items[].incumbent.identifier fields on the superseded @ogframework.com address -- so the charter that ratified the addressing convention did not itself follow it. Corrected: strategist and implementer incumbent identifiers now og-strategist@ogframework.orgdef and og-implementer@ogframework.orgdef. The distinction applied: incumbent.identifier is CURRENT STATE and must track the ratified convention, whereas staffed_via narrative, authors[] and history[] are DATED RECORDS and keep their as-of-their-time identities (no retro-rebrand) -- which is why lines carrying @ogframework.com and @oagp.org elsewhere in this file are correct and were deliberately left alone. Recorded as its own version rather than silently patched into v0.3.0, since v0.3.0 was already pushed. Also surfaced by the same orient and NOT fixed here, because it needs a ratified convention rather than an edit: 26 memos carry action_required true, nearly all long discharged, so the substrate can enumerate ever-actioned items but not OPEN ones -- a defect against the enumerable property that v0.3.0 itself made normative (A2.4). Proposal to follow." }
    ]
  }
}
